we mainly restarted because of issue #26 and #24:
    "max_arity hardcoded to 8 is too low for large structures"
    -> already structurally fixed here: FUNCTOR.arity is int32_t, argument
       cells are just contiguous heap cells, no fixed-size array anywhere.
       confirm this stays true - don't reintroduce a compile-time cap
       when adding compound-term builtins.
    "dev branch may be able to move more of the logic to Prolog"

closed github issues = bugs already found and fixed once - don't
reintroduce when porting/reimplementing the same feature:
    #23 current_prolog_flag/2 must return integers for max_integer/
        min_integer/max_arity, not atoms
    #22 -f means fast startup (skip ~/.trilog), not something else
    #20 read_from_chars/2, read_term_from_chars/3, write_term_to_chars/3 -
        chars, not atoms, as the text representation (reclaimed faster)
    #19 false/0 must exist as a builtin
    #16 atom '1' must read back as the atom '1', not the integer 1
    #15 undefined predicate -> existence_error(procedure, Name/Arity),
        not silent failure
    #14 double-quoted string chars that look like digits ('1') must stay
        chars, not get coerced to integers
    #13 current_prolog_flag(F,V) must enumerate all pairs on backtracking
        when F is unbound; type_error is wrong for an atom that's just
        not a valid flag - domain_error is correct (8.17.2.2 b)
    #12 writeq/1 must escape control chars properly (writeq('\n') -> '\n')
    #11 "abc" must read as a list of one-char atoms (chars), not codes
    #4  functor(X,Y,Z) with X,Y,Z all unbound, or X is Y with Y unbound,
        must throw instantiation_error, not fail
    #1  [L|Ls] = "abc" must unify against a double-quoted string like any
        other list - string representation must actually be a list

still-open issues, relevant if the feature area comes up:
    #28 top-level answer sequence interruption not indicated
    #27 readability: allow more chars in predicate names
    #7  number_chars/2 flagged as a good correctness baseline to start
        parsing from
    #24 dev branch note: more logic could move to Prolog (this restart's
       whole premise)

known bugs from old trilog's own TODO, found via test/ulrich/ and
test/iso_quad.pl - re-verify these can't happen in the new heap/arena
design before considering a feature "done":
    - builtin_atom_concat: stack-use-after-return once the concatenated
      atom got large (old MAX_NAME 16k) - triggered by ulrich/select_quad.pl
    - term.c make_var: MAX_VARS table exhaustion was a hard abort()
    - sub_atom/atom_concat split by byte offset, not UTF-8 char offset -
      can produce invalid truncated multi-byte sequences
    - no occurs-check, no cycle detection: self-referential unification
      (member(X,X), select(E,Xs,Xs)) hangs or crashes the printer
